WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 10.10 · Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk
Policy management and review

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Policies protect people only when they are approved, known, followed and kept up to date.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:24.059
Policy management is the simple cycle that keeps each policy approved, known, followed and up to date. Without it, even good policies stop protecting people.

4
00:00:24.459 --> 00:00:25.059
The policy cycle

5
00:00:25.059 --> 00:00:36.759
Draft and consult: Write the policy, then ask the people it affects what is unclear or missing. For example: The founders draft a trainee policy and ask two trainees what is unclear.

6
00:00:36.759 --> 00:00:45.867
Approve and share: Approve it, share it, train people and collect acknowledgements. For example: Each new trainee confirms reading the code of conduct during onboarding.

7
00:00:45.867 --> 00:00:58.026
Check and review: Check it is followed, then review on schedule and after any big change. For example: The bakery reviews safeguarding every year, and again after its first concern.

8
00:00:58.426 --> 00:00:59.026
Why the cycle matters

9
00:00:59.026 --> 00:01:05.070
1. Funders, regulators and insurers may ask what applied at a given time.

10
00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:10.004
2. Out-of-date policies can mislead people when it matters most.

11
00:01:10.004 --> 00:01:15.567
3. Acknowledgements show that people actually know the rules.

12
00:01:15.967 --> 00:01:16.567
What your register records

13
00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:21.500
1. Version, status, owner, approver, approval date and next review.

14
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:27.174
2. Who must acknowledge each policy, and where the current copy lives.

15
00:01:27.174 --> 00:01:33.848
3. What changed and why at each review, with old versions archived.

16
00:01:34.248 --> 00:01:34.848
What to avoid

17
00:01:34.848 --> 00:01:39.041
Deleting old versions instead of archiving them.

18
00:01:39.041 --> 00:01:44.715
Reviewing only on schedule, not after incidents, law changes or registration.

19
00:01:44.715 --> 00:01:50.648
Changing a policy without telling the people it affects.

20
00:01:51.248 --> 00:01:53.048
You set up your policy register and review schedule.

21
00:01:53.048 --> 00:01:57.048
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:01:58.548 --> 00:02:01.648
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
